### ShowTime - Catalog API (run from IntelliJ: click the green arrow next to each request)
### Requests go through the gateway on :8080. Tokens come from Keycloak on :8180.

### 1. Get a token for the partner test user (password grant = dev only)
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/showtime/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=showtime-web&username=partner1&password=partner1

> {% client.global.set("partnerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 2. Get a token for the admin test user
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/showtime/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=showtime-web&username=admin1&password=admin1

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Cities (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/cities

### Shows in Mumbai today (public). Add &date=2026-12-01 for another day.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/shows?city=MUM

### One show with prices (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/shows/1

### Seat layout of screen 1 (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/screens/1/layout

### Movies only
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/contents?type=MOVIE

### Add a city (ADMIN only)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "DEL", "name": "Delhi" }

### My venues (partner)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/venues/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}

### Add a screen with a seat layout to venue 1 (owner partner or admin)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/venues/1/screens
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Audi 2",
  "rows": [
    { "label": "A", "seats": 10, "category": "REGULAR" },
    { "label": "B", "seats": 10, "category": "REGULAR" },
    { "label": "C", "seats": 8,  "category": "PREMIUM" }
  ]
}

### Schedule a show (fails with 409 if it overlaps another show on that screen)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/shows
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contentId": 1,
  "screenId": 1,
  "startsAt": "2026-12-20T22:30:00+05:30",
  "prices": { "REGULAR": 300, "PREMIUM": 450, "RECLINER": 800 }
}

### Try as a customer: expect 403
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/showtime/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=showtime-web&username=customer1&password=customer1

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/catalog/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "PUN", "name": "Pune" }

### Skeleton services through the gateway (Phase 1 replaces these)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/inventory/status

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/status

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/payments/status
